  "id": "leverlaneboatyard",
  "note": "LEVER LANE BOATYARD — a boat shed on Lever Lane, a quarter of a mile from any water.\n\nThe tile's prose: doors tall enough to walk a mast through, not fully opened in living memory;\nLEVER LANE BOATYARD cut into a plank above them in letters that took someone a whole winter; through the\ngap, the ribs of something big and unfinished.\n\nSo it is a tall timber shed under a shallow barrel roof, the street face almost all door: two\nleaves the full height, standing a hand's width apart, with the gap lit from inside, and the plank\nwith the name over them. High clerestory windows run down both flanks to light the hull, and a\nlean-to workshop sits against the back.\n\nIt stands in for the `hulls` arm (`replaces`), which stays in LEGACY_MODELS.",
  "pal": "ty_oc_board",
  "replaces": "hulls",
